# Single-Module Navigation (Navigation 3)

This project uses **Navigation 3**, not Navigation 2 / Navigation Compose
(`NavHost`, `NavController`, `composable<Route>`). Do not add
`androidx.navigation:navigation-compose`.

Keep Navigation 3, AGP, Kotlin, and Compose BOM versions from
`gradle/libs.versions.toml`. Do not downgrade them to match older skill
templates.

## Navigation Structure

```
presentation/navigation/
├── AppNavHost.kt         # NavDisplay + bottom bar
├── Routes.kt             # NavKey destinations
└── NavExtensions.kt      # back-stack helpers
```

## Route definitions

Every destination is a `@Serializable` type that implements `NavKey`:

```kotlin
// presentation/navigation/Routes.kt
package com.mascill.healthtrack.presentation.navigation

import androidx.navigation3.runtime.NavKey
import kotlinx.serialization.Serializable

@Serializable
data object HomeRoute : NavKey

@Serializable
data object PracticeRoute : NavKey

@Serializable
data class ConversationRoute(val conversationId: String) : NavKey
```

## NavDisplay setup

```kotlin
// presentation/navigation/AppNavHost.kt
@Composable
fun AppNavHost(modifier: Modifier = Modifier) {
    val backStack = rememberNavBackStack(HomeRoute)

    NavDisplay(
        backStack = backStack,
        onBack = { backStack.navigateBack() },
        modifier = modifier,
        entryDecorators = listOf(
            rememberSaveableStateHolderNavEntryDecorator(),
            rememberViewModelStoreNavEntryDecorator(),
        ),
        entryProvider = entryProvider {
            entry<HomeRoute> {
                HomeScreen(
                    onOpenConversation = { id ->
                        backStack.navigateTo(ConversationRoute(id))
                    },
                )
            }
            entry<ConversationRoute> { key ->
                ConversationScreen(
                    conversationId = key.conversationId,
                    onBackClick = { backStack.navigateBack() },
                )
            }
        },
    )
}
```

Required libraries:

```kotlin
implementation(libs.androidx.navigation3.runtime)
implementation(libs.androidx.navigation3.ui)
implementation(libs.androidx.lifecycle.viewmodel.navigation3)
implementation(libs.kotlinx.serialization.json)
```

`rememberViewModelStoreNavEntryDecorator()` scopes a `ViewModel` to the
`NavEntry`. Screens keep using:

```kotlin
import androidx.hilt.lifecycle.viewmodel.compose.hiltViewModel

@Composable
fun HomeScreen(
    viewModel: HomeViewModel = hiltViewModel(),
)
```

Do not import `androidx.hilt.navigation.compose.hiltViewModel`
(Navigation 2).

## Back-stack helpers

```kotlin
// presentation/navigation/NavExtensions.kt
fun MutableList<NavKey>.navigateTo(key: NavKey) {
    add(key)
}

fun MutableList<NavKey>.navigateBack() {
    if (size > 1) removeLastOrNull()
}

fun MutableList<NavKey>.navigateToTopLevel(key: NavKey) {
    if (lastOrNull() == key) return
    add(key)
    while (firstOrNull() != key) {
        removeAt(0)
    }
}
```

- `navigateTo` — push a screen (chat, detail)
- `navigateBack` — pop; keep at least the start destination
- `navigateToTopLevel` — switch a bottom-nav tab and drop nested keys

There is no `NavController`. Pass `backStack` (or a lambda like
`onOpenConversation`) into screens.

## Bottom navigation

```kotlin
val currentKey = backStack.lastOrNull()

NavigationBar {
    BottomNavItem.entries.forEach { item ->
        val selected = currentKey == item.key
        NavigationBarItem(
            selected = selected,
            onClick = { backStack.navigateToTopLevel(item.key) },
            icon = { Icon(item.icon, contentDescription = item.label) },
            label = { Text(item.label) },
        )
    }
}
```

Use a single `rememberNavBackStack` until a screen actually needs an
independent tab back stack. Multiple back stacks
(`rememberDecoratedNavEntries`) can wait until then.

## Adding a screen

1. Add a `NavKey` to `Routes.kt`
2. Add `entry<YourRoute>` in `AppNavHost`
3. Push with `backStack.navigateTo(YourRoute(...))`

## Do not use

```kotlin
// Navigation 2 — not this project
NavHost(...) { composable<HomeRoute> { } }
navController.navigate(HomeRoute)
navController.popBackStack()
```
